<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin congratulates Clinton.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin congratulates Clinton.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian President Boris Yeltsin, just a day after coming through open heart surgery, sent Bill Clinton a message of congratulations on his reelection to the White House on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A Kremlin spokesman confirmed a report by Interfax news agency, which said Yeltsin told Clinton, whom he likes to call &quot;my friend Bill&quot;, that he hoped relations would continue to develop in a spirit of genuine partnership and cooperation.</p>
<p>Clinton had wished Yeltsin a speedy recovery before he underwent multiple heart bypass surgery on Tuesday. Doctors said on Wednesday they were pleased with Yeltsin's progress.</p>
</text>
